                <pb facs="0768" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1640: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-07T22:00:00+01:00">October 7, 1935—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 8—12:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>442. A communiqué was issued this afternoon giving the following text of a
                    telegram dated October 7 from the Ethiopian Foreign Minister to the Secretary
                    General: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Italian troops escorted by 20 airplanes entered Aduwa yesterday without
                            resistance after taking Adigrat. Our troops which were outside the town
                            of Aduwa are still there. All engagements hitherto have been with our
                            frontier guard and small isolated detachments. Our troops have not yet
                            gone into action. Italian aggression, in preparation for several months
                            against Ethiopia which has been systematically refused arms for its
                            defense, has thus been carried into effect in a district where the
                            frontier has been clearly defined by the treaties and is therefore
                            indisputable.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
